  "a_footnotes": "(1) 2012 operating profit and consolidated income before income taxes exclude the impact of an increase in pension expense due to a mark-to-market loss recognized outside of a 10% corridor of $4.831 billion, allocated between the U.S. Domestic Package segment ($3.177 billion), International Package segment ($941 million), and Supply Chain & Freight segment ($713 million). 2012 also excludes an $896 million pre-tax charge from the withdrawal liability associated with restructuring a multiemployer pension plan in the U.S. Domestic Package segment. 2011 operating profit and consolidated income before income taxes exclude the impact of an increase in pension expense due to a mark-to-market loss recognized outside of a 10% corridor of $827 million, allocated between the U.S. Domestic Package segment ($479 million), International Package segment ($171 million), and Supply Chain & Freight segment ($177 million). 2011 operating profit and consolidated income before income taxes also excludes a $33 million gain on certain real estate transactions ($15 million loss in U.S. Domestic Package and a $48 million gain in Supply Chain & Freight). (2) 2012 net income and earnings per share amounts exclude the after tax impact of the adjustments described in (1), which combined to a decrease in net income by $3.582 billion. 2011 net income and earnings per share amounts exclude the after tax impact of the adjustments described in (1), which combined to a decrease net income by $507 million."
